From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz.majnert@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:33:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] task: refuse an interpreter reset unless the machine is idle

EMC_TASK_PLAN_INIT re-initialises the interpreter at once: it reloads the
INI settings and runs RS274NGC_STARTUP_CODE, whatever task is doing. On a
machine that is still running an MDI command, a dwell, queued motion or a
jog, that silently swaps the modes underneath work in progress.

Check in emcTaskPlan(), where task handles the command, that the
interpreter, task, the MDI queue and motion are all at rest, and refuse the
reset with an operator error otherwise. Because task is single threaded and
owns this state, no other client can start work between the check and the
reset.

The new test tests/task/interp-reset-requires-idle checks that resets are
refused during an MDI move, a dwell and a jog without touching the modes,
and accepted again once the machine is idle.
